          %h2#References References
          %p
            The idea of defining étale morphisms
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            as those that get send to a pullback square by a natural transformation goes back to lectures by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andr%C3%A9+Joyal"} André Joyal
            in the 1970s.
          %p See the introduction and see section 4 of
          %ul#Dubuc
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Eduardo+Dubuc"}> Eduardo Dubuc
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %em Axiomatic etal maps and a theory of spectrum
          %p
            The identification of the natural transformation in question with that induced by an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+triple"} adjoint triple
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Q-categories"}> Q-categories
            ”) and the relation to
            %em formal
            étaleness is observed (apparently independently?) in
          %ul#KontsevichRosenbergSpaces
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Maxim+Kontsevich"}> Maxim Kontsevich
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Rosenberg"} Alexander Rosenberg
              = succeed "," do
                %em Noncommutative spaces
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/KontsevichRosenbergNCSpaces.pdf", :title => "pdf"} pdf
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "http://www.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/preprints/send?bid=2331"} ps
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "http://www.mpim-bonn.mpg.de/preprints/send?bid=2303"} dvi
          %p
            Formalization and discussion in the context of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cohesive+%28%E2%88%9E%2C1%29-toposes"} cohesive (∞,1)-toposes
            is in section 2.5.3 (and defn 5.3.19) of
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Urs+Schreiber"}> Urs Schreiber
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/schreiber/show/differential+cohomology+in+a+cohesive+topos"} differential cohomology in a cohesive topos
